          "path": "_m/g/c/p/v/waterloo-bridge-wp/antony-gormley-on-the-horizon-.jpg",
          "filename": "Antony Gormley on the horizon - geograph.org.uk - 453004.jpg",
          "caption": "Antony Gormley on the horizon The lifesize figures cast from the artist's own body are part of the 'Event Horizon' installation associated with his 2007 exhibition at the Hayward Gallery. As well as the two on the left here, and one on the bridge, right, alongside the  taxi, the figures are positioned near and far within a 1.5km radius around the gallery, some no more than tiny shapes on highrise buildings beyond the river. It is impossible to see them all from one viewpoint: the most I managed was 13.",
          "alt": "Antony Gormley on the horizon The lifesize figures cast from the artist's own body are part of the 'Event Horizon' installation associated with his 2007 exhibition at the Hayward Gallery. As well as the two on the left here, and one on the bridge, right, alongside the  taxi, the figures are positioned near and far within a 1.5km radius around the gallery, some no more than tiny shapes on highrise buildings beyond the river. It is impossible to see them all from one viewpoint: the most I managed was 13.",
